## Undetermined provenance: `libvoxel.wasm`

`go2_robot_sdk/external_lib/libvoxel.wasm` is a 9.5 KB WebAssembly binary that
decodes the Go2's LIDAR voxel format. It is loaded at runtime by
`go2_robot_sdk/go2_robot_sdk/infrastructure/sensors/lidar_decoder.py`.

It was added upstream on 2024-02-29 with no stated origin, no author, and no
license. It carries no license grant of any kind, and this repository cannot
establish one. It is retained here because removing it disables LIDAR decoding,
and it is flagged rather than silently redistributed.

Anyone redistributing this repository should treat this file as an open question
and consider one of: obtaining clarification from the upstream project, fetching
it at build time from upstream instead of vendoring it, or removing it and the
LIDAR decode path.

**This is an open-source-release blocker, not a documentation item.** An
undetermined-license binary that is executed at runtime cannot be cleared by
disclosure. It needs an OSPO decision, and that has the longest lead time of any
open item in this repository — raise it before anything else.

Integrity, meanwhile, is pinned. `lidar_decoder.py` verifies the file's SHA-256
against `LIBVOXEL_SHA256` and refuses to instantiate the module on a mismatch, so
the bytes that execute are the bytes reviewed here:

```
SHA-256  1ba27f065199954dc562b233aa38ea775ac687118cce77b5c71bc14e17e05542
Size     9,520 bytes
```

That fixes tampering and corruption. It does not fix provenance.

